WEBVTT

00:00:00.158 --> 00:00:03.647
Welcome to Module 10, Reshaping Data in PostgreSQL.

00:00:03.647 --> 00:00:07.427
Reshaping changes structure, not the underlying facts.

00:00:07.427 --> 00:00:14.772
We will move between long and wide forms, pivot categories into columns, unpivot columns back into rows,

00:00:14.772 --> 00:00:19.232
preserve meaningful NULL values, and protect the intended analytical grain.

00:00:19.232 --> 00:00:26.097
The most important habit in this module is to say what one output row represents before you write the reshape

00:00:26.097 --> 00:00:32.312
query. Keep a real project in mind as we work through this section—for example,

00:00:32.312 --> 00:00:35.542
a BI dashboard turning monthly categories into presentation columns.

00:00:35.542 --> 00:00:43.152
The technical feature matters because it changes what questions we can answer reliably and how easily another

00:00:43.152 --> 00:00:45.002
analyst can understand our work.

00:00:45.002 --> 00:00:51.972
As you listen, try to connect each SQL or data concept to a decision you might need to defend later:

00:00:51.972 --> 00:00:55.377
what the data means, what one row represents, what can be missing,

00:00:55.377 --> 00:00:59.600
and what assumptions the transformation introduces.
